  "about": "Computed styles' storage (generate.mjs writes CssProperty.hx, CssProperties.hx and CssGroups.hx from it): every stored longhand in one group, a group inherited or not as all its properties are, so an element shares its parent's inherited groups and the initial reset ones unless something in them is set. impact: what a change to the property redoes (layout; text: inherited text that lays text out again; paint; composite: opacity and transforms; none: no rendering), the group's unless a property says otherwise. kinds: a property whose typed value isn't what its grammar suggests. Logical properties have ids but no storage: the cascade maps them to their physical ones (horizontal-tb, by direction).",
